pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: the same wrapped watcher slack at the i128 width, which `--kernel-verify`
% does not model. `i128::MAX ~x1 >= -1` is trivially true but its slack `i128::MAX + 1`
% wrapped to i128::MIN, so ~x1 was reported as an assignment-independent propagation and
% conflicted with the unit `1 x1 >= 1`. The formula is satisfiable (x1 true).
f 2 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
